   "response_text": "I found it! Look at lines 186-188:\n\n```python\nmcfg = config[\"model\"]\ninput_dim = X_train.shape[1]\ninput_dim = mcfg.get(\"input_dim\", input_dim)\n```\n\nThe code first gets the actual input dimension from the loaded data (`X_train.shape[1]`), but then it **overrides** it with `mcfg.get(\"input_dim\", input_dim)`. This means if `input_dim` is specified in the config, it will use that instead of the actual data dimension.\n\nLooking at the config:\n```yaml\n\"input_dim\": 10\n```\n\nBut the error shows the actual input is 105 (256x105). The issue is clear:\n- The actual data has 105 input features (10 base + 95 aux features from the data loading logic)\n- But the config specifies `input_dim: 10`\n- The model is created with only 10 input dimensions\n- When the actual 105-dimensional data is passed to the model, it fails\n\nLet me verify this by checking the data utility:",
